    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Investigate with AI\r\n\r\nUse AI Chat to see how its interpretation of data compares to your own.  \r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. **Add the PDF** for the dataset from your station into AI Chat.  \r\n   *(Each dataset represents real sensor or system data from a career scenario — like the Zookeeper or Concert Promoter.)*\r\n\r\n2. **Write your own prompt** to ask the AI what it thinks the data shows.  \r\n   - Try describing what kind of data it is and what you want the AI to look for.  \r\n   - Press **Send** and read the AI’s response.\r\n\r\n3. Compare the AI’s interpretation to your own labels in the **Activity Guide.**  \r\n   - Did the AI describe the data the same way you did?  \r\n   - What details did it notice or miss?\r\n\r\n4. Record your thoughts in the **Investigate with AI** section of your Activity Guide.\r\n\r\n::: details [**Need help with your prompt?**]\r\nTry starting with something like:\r\n> What do you think this data shows?  \r\n> What patterns or problems do you notice in this dataset?  \r\n> Could any of these readings or messages mean something different?\r\n:::",
    "aichat_settings": {
      "initialCustomizations": {
        "selectedModelId": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "temperature": 0.5,
        "systemPrompt": "",
        "retrievalContexts": [

        ],
        "modelCardInfo": {
          "botName": "Investigate with AI Assistant",
          "description": "This AI tool helps students explore how humans and AI interpret data differently.\nStudents upload a small, “messy” dataset from a real-world scenario (such as animal monitoring, museum sensors, or crowd data) and ask the AI to explain what it sees. The AI describes patterns, possible problems, and uncertainties in the data—then asks students to compare their own interpretations.\n\nBy discussing how their thinking differs from the AI’s, students learn how human decisions and labeling choices shape how computer systems use data.",
          "intendedUse": "Who It’s For: Middle school students learning about sensors, data, and human roles in AI systems.\n\nWhat It Does:\n\nInterprets short, ambiguous datasets provided in class.\n\nPoints out possible patterns or problems it detects.\n\nEncourages students to share their own analysis and compare reasoning.\n\nPrompts reflection about how human labeling and context affect AI performance.",
          "limitationsAndWarnings": "AI Can Be Uncertain: The model may make reasonable guesses based on patterns but can’t truly “see” or “hear” the data.\n\nSimplified Reasoning: Its explanations are designed for discussion, not technical accuracy.\n\nNot a Real Diagnostic Tool: Interpretations are for learning and exploration only, not real-world decision-making.",
          "testingAndEvaluation": "Accuracy: Does the AI provide a plausible interpretation of the dataset?\nClarity: Are explanations short, friendly, and age-appropriate?\nReflection Quality: Does the conversation encourage students to think critically about human vs. AI perspectives?",
          "exampleTopics": [
            "What patterns do you notice in this dataset?",
            "Why do you think the sensor readings dropped here?",
            "Could this missing data mean something else?",
            "Do you think my labels make sense?",
            "What might happen if an AI misread this data?"
          ],
          "isPublished": false
        }
      },
      "visibilities": {
        "selectedModelId": "hidden",
